        "collapsible_tab_AN6y99": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "About Nationally Recognised Course",
            "icon": "star",
            "content": "<p>This is the highest qualification available in Australia and has been designed to give you all the skills and competency required to begin testing and tagging. This course has been completed by individuals, large corporations and thousands of small and medium-sized businesses.</p><h3>Units of Competency</h3><p>By completing the Nationally Recognised Course you will receive a statement of attainment for UEESS00174 - Electrical Safety Testing of Electrical Cord Connected Equipment and Cord Assemblies Skill Set.<br/> <br/>This Skill Set contains the following Units of Competency which you will complete as part of this course:<br/> <br/><strong>UEECD0007</strong> - Apply work health and safety regulations, codes and practices in the workplace<br/> <br/><strong>UEERL0003</strong> - Conduct in-service safety testing of electrical cord connected equipment and cord assemblies</p><ul><li><strong>Costs:</strong> $495 GST Exempt</li><li><strong>Duration:</strong> 1 day face-to-face (8-9 hours), plus online WHS component (3-4 hours)</li><li><strong>Locations</strong>: North Parramatta, Penrith</li><li><strong>Qualifications Received:</strong> Statements of Attainment & ID card with Certificate No.</li><li><strong>Qualification Level:</strong> Highest level (ASQA approved)</li><li><strong>Electrical knowledge:</strong> No previous electrical knowledge or background is required</li></ul>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_t9AL73": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "About Short Course (Non-Accredited)",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "content": "<p>The Short Course meets the minimum requirements set by AS/NZS 3760 and still allows you to freely test and tag as you wish. Although it also involves learning the same information, it has some minor differences:</p><ul><li>No OHS component</li><li>Issued with Certificate of Attendance</li></ul>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_RUBEc8": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Course Detail",
            "icon": "clipboard",
            "content": "<p>Test & Tag Training is NSW's go-to-expert for fully accredited test and tag courses. With 18 years of experience as an RTO, our commitment to lifetime support and excellence ensures you have the skills and knowledge to succeed in testing and tagging.</p><p>For any courses in NSW, the day runs from approx. 8:00am to 4:30pm.<br/><br/>On the day you'll be provided with everything you need, which includes a manual, pen, notepad and equipment to use (you can also bring your own portable appliance tester).<br/><br/>You will be shown how to use a PAT Tester in a small-sized class (strict maximum of 12 students) by our experienced test and tag industry specialist Russ. This will ensure you have an interactive learning experience and given all the help you need. The course comprises of both theory and practical, but with a heavy focus on practical hands-on work to ensure you're completely ready to test and tag on your own.<br/><br/>Once you have completed the course, we place an emphasis on giving you free lifetime support. We'll be there to provide any technical help you might require, whether it's by phone, email or video call. </p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_fmxizc": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Locations",
            "icon": "map_pin",
            "content": "<h3>North Parramatta:</h3><p>Uniting Venues,<br/>18 Masons Drive North Parramatta NSW 2151</p><h3>Penrith:</h3><p>Sydney International Regatta Centre,<br/>Gate A, Old Castlereagh Road Castlereagh NSW 2749</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_aUKp3U": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why Use Us",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "content": "<ul><li>We provide lifetime technical support after the course</li><li>Trained over 35,000 students in NSW</li><li>Our Nationally Recognised Course is fully accredited</li><li>We are a Registered Training Organisation</li><li>Our NSW instructors hold min. Cert IV in Training and Assessment</li><li>The most comprehensive test and tag course available</li><li>Special deals after the course if you would like to buy equipment or accessories</li><li>Highest rated (4.8/5) test and tag course in Australia</li></ul>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_PLAMRG": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Portable Appliance Testers (PAT)",
            "icon": "lightning_bolt",
            "content": "<p>Test and Tag Training will teach you how to use the latest and most popular Portable Appliance Testers on the Australian market.<br/><br/>For students looking to buy a new PAT, this will give you the opportunity to try a few different options and to choose the ideal one for your job. We stock a complete range of PAT Testers for you to try out.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
