    "collapsible_content_aqyrc4": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_jP3dUU": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What does a typical training day look like?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>The morning session will predominately focus on the theory required to test and tag, while the afternoon focuses heavily on learning to test and tag with a portable appliance tester. All of our classes in NSW are kept to a maximum of 12 people so that everyone in the room can get individual time and support from our trainer. Upon completing the course, you should be completely comfortable at testing and tagging on your own.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_JRcULQ": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Where are your training locations in NSW?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>We have two face-to-face training locations in NSW - North Parramatta and Penrith. </p><p>Our venue in North Parramatta generally runs once a week and Penrith every month.</p><p>If you're wanting to do a course somewhere else across Sydney, we also provide onsite training at your premises for a group of students. </p><p>Alternatively, our online course can be conducted from anywhere in NSW.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_9amYtn": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How is the Nationally Recognised course different to the Short course? ",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Both the Nationally Recognised and Short Courses are delivered in a face-to-face training session over 1 day. However, the major difference between them is that the Nationally Recognised Course has an additional self-paced OHS (Occupational Health and Safety) online component and is thereby considered the highest qualification (ASQA approved). The course you decide on will largely depend on your particular needs, but the vast majority of students will complete the Nationally Recognised one for a <a href=\"https://ttt-au.myshopify.com/pages/choosing-right-course\" title=\"Which Test & Tag Course Should I Choose?\">variety of reasons</a>.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_YAFc4k": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long does the course go for? ",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Our 1 day comprehensive course generally starts at 8:00 am and finishes at approximately 4:30 pm, with breaks for morning tea and lunch. If you’re planning on doing the Nationally Recognised course, it’ll consist of an additional self-paced WHS online component, which is to be completed in your own time before the course date. This typically takes around 3-4 hours to complete, depending on your existing knowledge. </p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_DhYd67": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Who will be the instructor on the day? ",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>All Test & Tag Courses in NSW are run by our experienced instructor Doug Steen. With over a decade of experience in teaching other people to test and tag, he has expert knowledge of the relevant test and tag regulations and best practices. </p><p>Doug is extremely approachable and will ensure you're given plenty of 1 on 1 time to ensure you're confident. We're sure you'll be extremely satisfied with Dough, as he consistently receives 5 star reviews and positive feedback for all of his test and tag courses. </p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_wgai4y": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What if I need technical support or help after the course? ",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>You’ll have the peace of mind knowing that we'll be there when you need us, whether it's by phone, email or in person. Every single student taught by Test & Tag Training receives free lifetime technical support from our team of experts. Guaranteed. This could be anything from how to use a specific appliance tester or how to test and tag a particular electrical appliance. We want to ensure we're making people's jobs easier by offering dependable service and expert advice when you need it most.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
